  "verified_facts": [
    "A HTTP 429 usage_limit_reached fails over to B in the same streaming and non-streaming client request: two upstream attempts, client HTTP 200.",
    "The immediate next new request uses B only; A has credential-wide and model cooldowns.",
    "With body resets_in_seconds=12 and Retry-After=2, A stays excluded at 3 seconds and is eligible at 12.3 seconds. Provider recovery alone does not clear cooldown.",
    "Body resets_at takes precedence over resets_in_seconds (14-second absolute reset versus 60-second relative reset). Without either body reset field, Retry-After=90 is ignored: the first fallback cooldown is approximately one second and recovered A is used at 1.3 seconds.",
    "A session previously pinned to A fails over and rebinds to B. After clearing A, the same session stays on B while a new session uses A.",
    "Both exhausted: original request returns upstream HTTP 429 usage_limit_reached; later requests return local HTTP 429 model_cooldown with reset timing and no upstream attempts. Body reset=3 seconds is floored to a 10-second cooldown: still fails at 4 seconds, succeeds at 10.4 seconds after the mock recovers.",
    "After a generated SSE delta, both an explicit quota error and a transport disconnect leave client HTTP 200 with an error event and no response.completed. Neither retries B within that stream.",
    "An in-stream quota error cools A and the next request uses B. A raw disconnect does not cool A in this test; successive new requests keep selecting A and failing.",
    "PATCH priority from 100 to 101 preserves cooldown. POST reset-quota clears it, permitting the next new request to use recovered A."
